                <pb facs="0996" n="880" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg880"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.51/82.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Saltillo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-05T10:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 5, 1914, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s August 4, 9 p.m. Can the Department fully confirm the entire
                    information given in this telegram? It is stated here that Chao himself was
                    executed prior to June 27, 7 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
